<title>UK: LPC-PCB Investments gets 150m stg to buy Forward.</title>
<headline>LPC-PCB Investments gets 150m stg to buy Forward.</headline>
<text>
<p>LONDON, March 3 (LPC) - PCB Investments, the company established by Hicks, Muse, Tate &amp; Furst Equity Fund to facilitate its acquisition of Forward Group, has received a 150 million stg loan to back its 129 million stg offer, according to Daniel Dross, vice president of Hicks Muse, Tate &amp; Furst Inc.</p>
<p>Chase Manhattan Bank is arranging the six-month credit which is priced at 250 bps over LIBOR. The company expects to refinance and extend the maturity on the credit within the next six months.</p>
<p>Hicks, Muse, Tate &amp; Furst Equity Fund 3 is a US private investment fund and Forward Group is a UK-based supplier of interconnection services to the electronics industry.</p>
<p>Sophy Tonder</p>
<p>LPC Newsroom 44-0171-542-8367</p>
</text>
